  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "From Yao tribe’s Immortal Gu House Divine Light Hall she flies out and greets Gong Wan Ting first, then Nu Er Qian. Nu Er Qian reads her nature as gentle, not proficient in fighting and killing, but specialized in healing, and takes that as a sign Yao tribe does not intend to put in much effort. Yao Huang appointed her; he is friends with Heavenly Lord Bai Zu and framed the blood battle martial competition as an explanation to Longevity Heaven while focusing on refining Gu. Beyond most Gu Immortals’ expectations she asks how she could command the Longevity Edict with Fairy Gong Wan Ting present, offers it three times, and only on the third offer does Gong Wan Ting accept as if forced.",
      "chapters": [
        1193
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
